HST Office: picture edits survive saving as .docx and .doc (brightness, contrast, transparency, gamma, colours, flip, rotation).

A picture edited on the Picture tab or in the Image dialog came back as it was inserted after saving as .docx or .doc
and reopening. The Word exports wrote only the draw mode, the horizontal flip, the rotation (DOCX) and the crop:

- DOCX lost brightness, contrast, transparency, gamma, the red/green/blue channels and the vertical flip, and an
  as-character picture turned by 90 degrees came back 4/3 larger (3 times when also resized out of proportion): its
  layout size is no bounding box, but the export scaled it as one.
- DOC lost the rotation, transparency, gamma and the colour channels; brightness together with contrast, or a
  washout or grey/black-and-white picture with them, came back changed (the reader converts such pictures with Word's
  formula).

Now every setting Word can store is written as a Word property and read back: DOCX a:lum (brightness or contrast),
a:alphaModFix (transparency, also read into the Writer picture now), a:xfrm flipV (read as a vertically flipped
Writer picture, no longer a shape turned by a half turn); DOC escher gamma and rotation (with Word's flip and anchor
rules; the reader gives the picture its rotation and unrotated frame). A rotated picture keeps its size when its frame is laid out unrotated (as character, or not laid out again).
What a format cannot store is applied to the written picture the way HST Office draws it, so the picture looks the
same reopened in HST Office and in Word, with those settings back at their defaults:
- DOCX: gamma, colour channels, invert, brightness together with contrast, a washout with brightness or contrast;
- DOC: transparency, colour channels, invert, brightness together with contrast, a washout with either.
An as-character picture with a border (an HST picture style) no longer becomes smaller on every .doc save: the
reader now adds the room of its borders and shadow, which the export takes off, to the frame size.
A linked picture stays linked and nothing is applied to it, as in Word: what Word keeps for a link is written as
its properties (DOCX a:lum also with both brightness and contrast, a:alphaModFix, the draw mode, flips, rotation;
DOC escher brightness, contrast, gamma, draw mode, flips, rotation; a watermark with brightness or contrast as the
brightness and contrast HST Office shows it with), gamma (DOCX), colour channels, invert and transparency (DOC) are
left out. The readers keep them as properties of the link: the DOCX reader no longer converts a linked picture with
both brightness and contrast (oox), and the escher reader now reads the picture settings of a linked picture it
does not load (msfilter), without converting it.

The logic is in new HST files (sw/source/filter/ww8/hst/hstpictureadjust.*, sw/source/writerfilter/hst/
hstpictureimport.*); the LibreOffice files only call them (oox and msfilter: one condition each).

Test: CppunitTest_sw_hst_image_edits_roundtrip (DOCX and DOC round trip per setting: kept properties, written XML,
applied pixels compared with HST Office's drawing, rotation and size of floating, inline and flipped pictures, size of a bordered inline picture over two saves, linked pictures in DOCX and DOC stay linked with their settings).
